97
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:16,960
In this podcast, we're going to answer a few questions about eagle-scout

98
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:20,960
and we're going to start that in scoutmastership in seven minutes or less

99
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:23,960
by discussing what actually makes an eagle-scout,

100
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:27,960
And I've got a couple of email questions to answer that relate to the subject.

101
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:29,960
So let's get started, shall we?

102
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,960
Yeah, I think we shall.

103
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:36,960
Scoutmastership in seven minutes or less.

104
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,960
If a group of scouters get together

105
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:50,960
and they're going to spend a few hours together on a camping trip or something like that,

106
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,960
and they've got time to sit around and talk,

107
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:57,960
that talk will eventually turn to the question of what makes an eagle-scout,

108
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,960
And I am going to give you the answer.

109
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,960
That's right.

110
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:08,960
This often discussed, much debated question has one simple answer:

111
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:13,960
What makes an eagle-scout is a scout completes the requirements

112
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,960
issued by the Boy Scouts of America

113
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:19,960
and is approved by a duly constituted board of review.

114
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:21,960
That's what makes an eagle-scout.

115
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,960
There's nothing more to it.

116
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:25,960
That is it.

117
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:29,960
So what about this often discussed and argued qualities

118
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:33,960
of an eagle-scout, like maturity and leadership ability

119
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:37,960
and active service and all of those things?

120
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:40,960
All of these are embodied in the requirements,

121
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:44,960
but they aren't requirements in and of themselves.

122
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,960
So let's take a look at maturity first.

123
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:49,960
There's quite a laundry list of things that indicate

124
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,960
the maturity of an eagle candidate.

125
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:54,960
If he's made it to a board of review for eagle-scout,

126
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:56,960
that means he's had the following experiences:

127
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,960
He's earned 21 merit badges at a minimum.

128
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:04,960
He served a minimum of 16 months in a position of responsibility.

129
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:11,960
He's been camping for a bare minimum of at least 24 nights.

130
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:15,960
He's proposed, planned and carried out an eagle service project

131
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:19,960
and he's had a minimum of seven scoutmaster conferences

132
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,960
and five boards of review.

133
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:25,960
Now, it's theoretically possible that a scout could hoodwink

134
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,960
all of his merit badge counselors,

135
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,960
all the members of his boards of review

136
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,960
and all the scouts and leaders who signed off

137
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:33,960
on his advancement requirements

138
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:37,960
and the scoutmaster at all of those scoutmaster conferences.

139
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:41,960
It is theoretically possible that he could somehow

140
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:46,960
surreptitiously convince them that he was a mature young man.

141
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:50,960
but there are many theoretical possibilities in life

142
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,960
and few of them are likely.

143
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:56,960
There are heated arguments sometimes over the chronological age

144
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,960
of an eagle candidate.

145
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,960
Some people think he's too young,

146
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,960
Some people think he's too old.

147
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,960
It's not important.

148
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:08,960
You should know by now that age and maturity

149
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,960
do not always go hand in hand.

150
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,960
I mean, if you've been listening to these podcasts,

151
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,960
that should be clear. I'm older than you

152
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:19,960
And oh well, you get the idea.

153
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,960
How about leadership ability?

154
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:24,960
Well, to get to an eagle board of review,

155
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:28,960
a scout has held positions of responsibility

156
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,960
for a minimum of 16 months.

157
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:32,960
He may have been a great leader,

158
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,960
He may have been very responsible,

159
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:39,960
He may have been somewhat less than the ideal leader

160
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:43,960
and he may have been somewhat less than ideally responsible.

161
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,960
If he's skated by doing a lackluster job,

162
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:49,960
that's not the fault of the candidate

163
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,960
so much as a failure of the leadership

164
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:54,960
that is supposed to be overseeing his work.

165
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:58,960
16 months is plenty of time to discuss

166
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,960
and mentor and coach and cajole

167
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:04,960
and encourage and train any scout.

168
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,960
If he hasn't shown up,

169
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,960
if he hasn't done what he's supposed to do

170
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,960
and we haven't taken action,

171
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:13,960
it's unconscionably unfair to ambush him

172
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:16,960
and say that his tenure in a position of responsibility

173
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,960
is not satisfactory.

174
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:20,960
How about active service?

175
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:22,960
Well, how can a scout do the things

176
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,960
that we've talked about

177
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,960
without being actively involved in scouts?

178
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,960
There's much more heat than light

179
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:32,960
in most discussions about what it means to be active.

180
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,960
I have the antidote for that.

181
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,960
There's very specific guidance about this

182
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:38,960
in the Guide to Advancement.

183
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,960
I'm not going to go into it now,

184
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:42,960
but there's a three-level test

185
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:46,960
for determining if a scout is active or not

186
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:49,960
and the view from a thousand feet. on that test,

187
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,960
it's determined that he's satisfied

188
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:53,960
the expectations of his unit.

189
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:56,960
He's done, and then there are other alternatives

190
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:58,960
if it is determined that somehow

191
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:02,960
he has not satisfied the expectations of his unit.

192
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,960
Check it out in the Guide to Advancement.

193
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:07,960
It's very clear and it's very easy to follow.

194
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:10,960
What about the often stated undue influence

195
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,960
of parents on an Eagle candidate?

196
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:15,960
I've had the privilege of presenting more than 50

197
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:18,960
and somewhat less than 100 Eagle badges.

198
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:21,960
To tell you the truth, I really lost count right around 40..

199
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:25,960
Of those scouts, of those somewhere between 50 and 100 scouts,

200
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:28,960
two may have had more help from their parents

201
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,960
than I would have liked,

202
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:33,960
But it didn't devalue becoming an Eagle scout.

203
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,960
It wasn't some tragic miscarriage of justice.

204
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:39,960
I would have just liked those particular parents

205
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,960
to back off for a little bit

206
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,960
and let the poor scout breathe.

207
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,960
You know what I'm saying.

208
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,960
It is theoretically possible that parents can step in

209
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,960
and do all the work for the scout,

210
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,960
write his proposals and his reports.

211
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,960
It's a theoretical possibility

212
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:55,960
but I've never seen it happen.

213
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,960
I've seen parents be a little overheated about this,

214
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,960
be a little over-involved about it

215
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,960
kind of helicopter around.

216
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:02,960
I wish they wouldn't,

217
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:06,960
But to my lights it did not seriously impact

218
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:09,960
the value of the process that the scout went through

219
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,960
towards becoming an Eagle.

220
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:13,960
Every scout who's ever earned the rank of Eagle

221
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,960
did it individually

222
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:18,960
and in the opinion of the people he was working with,

223
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:21,960
he met the requirements at that time.

224
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:24,960
So right now we've had a million plus

225
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,960
scouts become Eagle scouts

226
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,960
throughout the history of the Boy Scouts of America

227
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:31,960
And I will bet that in the case of at least half of them,

228
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:33,960
someone thought they probably didn't deserve it,

229
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:36,960
Or they were at least a little skeptical

230
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:39,960
about whether or not that particular scout

231
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:42,960
had achieved- really really achieved-

232
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,960
becoming an Eagle scout.

233
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,960
Our district advancement chair is an old

234
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,960
scouting buddy of mine

235
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:51,960
and he regularly gets phone calls or emails

236
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,960
that cast doubts on the suitability

237
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:56,960
of a particular Eagle candidate

238
00:13:56,960 --> 00:14:00,960
And his reply to the people who bring these concerns to him

239
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:02,960
is that they can appear at the border review

240
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:05,960
or they can prepare a letter to send to the border review.

241
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,960
but he is not the messenger

242
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:11,960
and he will certainly not permit anonymous accusations.

243
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,960
He tells me that nine out of 10 people

244
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:14,960
never follow up.

245
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,960
They are never convinced enough

246
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:19,960
to follow themselves and represent these concerns.

247
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:22,960
Now I've been around for a while

248
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,960
